        ],
        [
          "August 13, 1984",
          "Athletics Athletics, Men's 10,000 m",
          "Martti Vainio ( FIN ) ※",
          "",
          "-1",
          "",
          "−1",
          "On August 13, 1984, the IOC stripped Finnish long-distance runner Martti Vainio of his silver medal in the men's 10,000 m race after failing an anti-doping test. As a result, bronze medalist Mike McLeod of Great Britain was awarded silver, and Kenyan runner Michael Musyoki, who placed fourth in the competition, was awarded bronze. [ 37 ]"
        ],
        [
